{"type":"error","path":"elm.json","title":"EXTRA COMMA","message":["I ran into a problem with your elm.json file. I was partway through parsing a
JSON object when I got stuck here:

16|     "indirect": {}
17|   }
18| ,}
     ",{"bold":false,"underline":false,"color":"RED","string":"^"},"
I saw a comma right before I got stuck here, so I was expecting to see a field
name like ",{"bold":false,"underline":false,"color":"yellow","string":""type""}," or ",{"bold":false,"underline":false,"color":"yellow","string":""dependencies""}," next.

This error is commonly caused by trailing commas in JSON objects. Those are
actually disallowed by <https://json.org> so check the previous line for a
trailing comma that may need to be deleted.

",{"bold":false,"underline":true,"color":null,"string":"Note"},": Here is an example of a valid JSON object for reference:

    {
      ",{"bold":false,"underline":false,"color":"yellow","string":""name""},": ",{"bold":false,"underline":false,"color":"yellow","string":""Tom""},",
      ",{"bold":false,"underline":false,"color":"yellow","string":""age""},": ",{"bold":false,"underline":false,"color":"yellow","string":"42"},"
    }

Notice that (1) the field names are in double quotes and (2) there is no
trailing comma after the last entry. Both are strict requirements in JSON!"]}

